{"term":"datum","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:b1d3bbe59ba9f39c15","definition":"Something known or assumed as fact, and is made the basis of reasoning or inference which an intellectual system of any sort (such as knowledge or theoretical framework) is constructed.","example":"a datum of experience","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["chart datum","datum circle","datum line","datum plane","datum point","datum surface","metadatum","sense datum"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/datum#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:539028ebd6170ac4b5","definition":"Singular of data: A single recorded phenomenon, especially obtained by scientific work.","example":"Holonym: data set","pos":"noun","synonyms":["data point"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"form-of, singular","register":"form-of, singular","wordFamily":["chart datum","datum circle","datum line","datum plane","datum point","datum surface","metadatum","sense datum"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/datum#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:96e3800b2388b5892f","definition":"A point, line, plane, or surface with reference to which positions (such as elevations) are measured or indicated. (Examples include a permanent benchmark in leveling or mean sea level in a topographical survey).","example":"A geodetic datum is sometimes also called a benchmark.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["chart datum","datum circle","datum line","datum plane","datum point","datum surface","metadatum","sense datum"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/datum#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.